A||N||17||4UMLA1||2.8 vs 3.4||||6||
Z||000000||4UMLA1||12-29-2001||09:46 PM||||You know it is funny how some things just sorta happen to you.  I have been deciding on weather or not to get a 3.4 installed into my 88 GT or not, and today sorta laid the answer right out in front of me, I think, but I will let you guys decide that.  I saw this 88 GT going down the road and it was messing around with this old VW, needless to say it blew it off of the road, so I decided to have a go at it and see just what he was made of.  I got behind him and I saw him look out of his rear mirrow and smile, down shifted to 3 gear and got next to him egging him on a little. I heard him get on his car a little so I responded with a little of my own, blew him right off of the road, no problem at all.  I then slowed down a little and got luck and a light caught us. He pulled up to me and his friend looked over at me and laughed a little, I could hear him reving up as the light changed.  It was unreal, as soon as I hit 3 gear, he was already 2 car lengths behind me and getting farther away.  I slowed down and the guy pulled up next to me and his friend asked what I had in the car, I told him it was a 2.8 liter, he said that I was full of crap.  I asked him what he had in his car, he said a 3.4 liter, I just looked at him like he had lost his mind! We both pulled over because he wanted to look at my engine.  He looked at it and almost cryed, he couldn't beleive that he had just been walked on with a 2.8 liter.  I told him that the only changes that I have made to the engine were a K & N Air filter and a Hypertech Chip, he couldn't beleive it.  He said that the 3.4 is good for tourque, but top end isn't that great.  I asked him how much he paid for the installation and he said that it was around $3400.00.  The enging in his car was also used and some of Ed Parks guys put it in the car.<BR>This is my problem that I am looking at.  Since I beat the socks off this guy with a 3.4, instead of spending $3400.00 for a 3.4 and a used one at that, can't I just invest about $2000.00 into the 2.8 and make it a lot quicker and stronger than a 3.4?  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/luv4rez/images/10%20fiero%20gt%20.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||avengador1||12-29-2001||10:00 PM||||If your car is running that great, why mess with it. Pocket the money and wait till you blow the engine or wear it out to rebuild it. Remember if it aint broke don't fix it. You could do some more external mods to the engine to get more H.P. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||4UMLA1||12-29-2001||10:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by avengador1:<BR><B>You could do some more external mods to the engine to get more H.P.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have always heard that when you are stadting to give an engine mor HP, that you should start with the exhaust, is this true?  If so, what kind of an exhaust system could I put on my car to give it more HP?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroHarry||12-30-2001||09:30 AM||||4umla1,<BR>Have we met?<P>I dont recognize your car. You should come out to a club meeting sometime <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SIg1_2.jpg"> <B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||12-30-2001||09:41 AM||||I am going to be doing the 3.4. I am going to hop it up a little before I install it. <P>It could have been the driver too. He may not be skilled or the engine may not be tuned good.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||lou_dias||12-30-2001||01:38 PM||||his car probably isn't in tune.<BR>maybe he also put in that damn Crane .423/.423 cam, it's all torque and no HP.  Should have left the stock camaro cam or go with the GM performance cam.<P>However my 3.4 with that damn cam did pull strong an Mustangs over 100mph.||||reg||1
Z||000006||foxgapfiero||12-30-2001||02:18 PM||||I've just finished putting a 3.4 in my 86 GT 5-speed. I did nothing to the engine except put valve seals in the heads when I put the new engine together. The one thing I did do was Joe Wynman's chip in the computer. I did a quick install of the motor because the 2.8 was just about dead. Just putting the 3.4 in has been a huge difference in bottom end power and the top end hasn't been a disapointment either. Can't wait to do my exhaust manifolds this year. This thing should really pick up and scream then. With a mild cam and some slight head work with port matching the 3.4 should have been the next motor for the Fiero.  Just my 2 cents..<P>------------------<BR>Mark Hoagland<BR>86GT 3.4<BR>88GT T-Top<BR>85GT caddy v-8 next swap<BR>84SE trailer next project||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dan010||12-30-2001||06:54 PM||||At first I was very dissapointed, to think all the reading I have done, to find out that a good running 2.8 could have has much power as a 3.4. Would like to hear others that have done this swap give there opinions.<BR> This makes me wonder about the 3.1/3.2 stroker motors real power compared to the stock 3.4 motors.<BR> I will need to do some thing in the future to my 86gt. Try to read every tread on this subject, with very confussing results and opinions. But this is a great site!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Neal||12-30-2001||07:14 PM||||well my old 2.8 ran STRONG, but had the misfortune of snappign the crankshaft...<P>it has been a long time since i drove it BUT i now have all of 20km on my fresh 3.4, so it prolly doesnt have the rings seated yet, and i can tell you it WILL be much stronger than the 2.8 was.<P>In other words im impressed with my 3.4, and wouldnt hesitate to go with another.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cooter||12-30-2001||07:52 PM||||My stock 3.4 runs circles around my friend's 2 GTs- an 86/4 speed (80,000 mile car) and 88 GT/5 speed. Probably he thought you were an easy target and didn't expect you to jump on him so quick. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||4UMLA1||12-30-2001||10:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>Probably he thought you were an easy target and didn't expect you to jump on him so quick. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats what I really don't understand.  We got caught by a light and when the light turned green, that was it, all I saw of his car was a front licenses plate and lights.<BR>He said that Ed Parks did the work on the engine.  I would think if you are going to pay him $3500.00 to put the engine in the car that they would tune and set the engine up to run as strong as you wanted it to run.  I have heard that they don't put in cams or anything internal inside of the engine, they just take the parts needed from the 2.8 and install them on the 3.4, is that ture or will they do the insides also?<BR>His car had about 140,000 miles on it and mine is getting ready to turn 139,000 miles, so the miles really arent that much of a differance.<BR>I am just curious about all of this because I have been reading a lot in here and other sites about how strong the 3.4 is and just want to be sure of the swap before I stick that kind of money into it, but then again, I could stick that money into the 2.8 and make it a real screamer <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||5
Z||000011||Cooter||12-30-2001||10:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 4UMLA1:<BR><B> Thats what I really don't understand.  We got caught by a light and when the light turned green, that was it, all I saw of his car was a front licenses plate and lights.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When you line up beside a VW beetle, do you carefully watch the lights, bring the engine up to launch RPM's and go through the whole process of a good launch when you know the car is not much of a fight? His mindset might have been "I have a new 3.4, there is no need in going through the motions of a complete staging" He was probably just over confident and did not anticipate your ability to get the jump on him. Over the years, I have embarassed some strong cars at the stop light grand-prix with my stock Civic all by them not expecting the unexpected 7800 RPM launch and full throttle upshifts from the mighty 1.6 liter powerhouse  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||4UMLA1||12-31-2001||09:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B> When you line up beside a VW beetle, do you carefully watch the lights, bring the engine up to launch RPM's and go through the whole process of a good launch when you know the car is not much of a fight? His mindset might have been "I have a new 3.4, there is no need in going through the motions of a complete staging" He was probably just over confident and did not anticipate your ability to get the jump on him.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You see, thats the whole point.  I always thought that there was a tremendus differance in the power of the 2.8 compared to the 3.4, even if both of the engines were complete stock.  I would have thought that even if he knew I wanted a peice of him, which he did know, that he would have walked all over me, but he didn't and he couldn't.  Trust me I almost had a heart attack when I found out that he had a 3.4 in his car!<P>||||reg||14
Z||000013||87ECOsomething||12-31-2001||10:54 AM||||I had Ed Parks put a remanufactured 3.4 (bored to 3.6) into my '87 coupe.<P>For the money I spent, I'm not truly impressed with it.  Of course, I've been riding in BOILERMAKER's and BENGAL4's s/c 3800-powered Fieros lately.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||13
