Z||000015||lou_dias||12-31-2001||04:36 PM||||from a hp comparison stock vs. stock it's only 20hp at the flywheel (some claim less due to the Fiero intake holding less volume) but if your 2.8 car has no options and his 3.4 is loaded and weighs 300lbs more than yours, then you are going to win.<P>the 3.4 really responds to head and intake porting and polishing and a bigger throttle body||||reg||1
Z||000016||4UMLA1||12-31-2001||05:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lou_dias:<BR><B>from a hp comparison stock vs. stock it's only 20hp at the flywheel (some claim less due to the Fiero intake holding less volume) but if your 2.8 car has no options and his 3.4 is loaded and weighs 300lbs more than yours, then you are going to win.<P>the 3.4 really responds to head and intake porting and polishing and a bigger throttle body</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||10
Z||000017||LoW_KeY||12-31-2001||06:09 PM||||Ohh yeah.. I heard from having a good driver changing to 24 lb and getting the computer chip re-programmed he was running a 13.8 out of it.<P>Not bad at all.. I plan to go through my 3.4 engine so anyone at the fiero show in MI next year wants a ride lemme know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
